    "b-studio-handlers-decision-6": {
      "id": "b-studio-handlers-decision-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": backend logic lives in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "packages/studio/server/",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/studio/server",
              "label": "packages/studio/server/"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " as shared Node handlers ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "canvas-file-api.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "agent-proxy.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "evals-api.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ") that the Vite dev server and the Electron shell both mount, so web and desktop behave identically. New API surfaces join "
        },
        {
          "insert": "server/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " as shared handlers, never as shell-specific code."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-studio-handlers-why-7": {
      "id": "b-studio-handlers-why-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "the rejected alternative was per-shell backends, which fork persistence behavior between web and desktop and double every fix."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-studio-handlers-applies-8": {
      "id": "b-studio-handlers-applies-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "packages/studio/server/",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/studio/server",
              "label": "packages/studio/server/"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", including every future API surface."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-studio-watch-decision-15": {
      "id": "b-studio-watch-decision-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": external-change notification is a shared module, "
        },
        {
          "insert": "packages/studio/server/canvas-file-watch.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/studio/server/canvas-file-watch.ts",
              "label": "packages/studio/server/canvas-file-watch.ts"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", that turns file events into "
        },
        {
          "insert": "canvas:file-changed",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " payloads and takes its transport from the shell. The Vite dev server wires it to its file watcher and HMR channel in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "vite.config.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". The Electron shell mounts "
        },
        {
          "insert": "canvas-file-api.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " without it, so desktop has the revision check and no live reload. This is the one current exception to identical web and desktop behavior."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-studio-watch-why-16": {
      "id": "b-studio-watch-why-16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": the file API reports the hash of each write through "
        },
        {
          "insert": "onCanvasWrite",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " before the write lands. The notifier uses that record to tell Studio's own saves from external writers. With the filter in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "server/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", a shell supplies only a watcher and a way to reach the client."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-studio-watch-applies-17": {
      "id": "b-studio-watch-applies-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "packages/studio/server/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", including a future Electron watcher, which calls the same notifier instead of adding shell-specific filtering."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-studio-dev-flag-decision-9": {
      "id": "b-studio-dev-flag-decision-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": development-only surfaces gate behind "
        },
        {
          "insert": "src/dev-flag.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/studio/src/dev-flag.ts",
              "label": "src/dev-flag.ts"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and live under "
        },
        {
          "insert": "src/dev/",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/studio/src/dev",
              "label": "src/dev/"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " (the dev rail, the evals page). Production routes never mount them unflagged."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-studio-dev-flag-why-10": {
      "id": "b-studio-dev-flag-why-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "the rejected alternative was shipping dev tooling unconditionally, which leaks internal surfaces into the product and blurs which routes are contract."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-studio-dev-flag-applies-11": {
      "id": "b-studio-dev-flag-applies-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "src/dev/",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/studio/src/dev",
              "label": "src/dev/"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", including every future dev surface."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-studio-surfaces-decision-12": {
      "id": "b-studio-surfaces-decision-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": client code groups by surface. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "src/agent/",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/studio/src/agent",
              "label": "src/agent/"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is for the agent session rail, "
        },
        {
          "insert": "src/project/",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/studio/src/project",
              "label": "src/project/"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " for project-board integration, "
        },
        {
          "insert": "src/style/",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/studio/src/style",
              "label": "src/style/"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " for the workspace style rail, and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "src/dev/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " for flagged dev tooling. Each owns its components, state, and adapters, and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "App.tsx",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " stays thin route wiring."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-studio-surfaces-why-13": {
      "id": "b-studio-surfaces-why-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": the rejected alternative was a flat component pile behind the router. The pile hides which code serves which surface and makes a surface impossible to remove cleanly."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-studio-surfaces-applies-14": {
      "id": "b-studio-surfaces-applies-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "packages/studio/src/",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/studio/src",
              "label": "packages/studio/src/"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", including every future studio surface, which gets its own folder rather than accreting into "
        },
        {
          "insert": "App.tsx",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-studio-style-decision-19": {
      "id": "b-studio-style-decision-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": the Style rail ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "StyleRail.tsx",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/studio/src/style/StyleRail.tsx",
              "label": "StyleRail.tsx"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ") is generated from "
        },
        {
          "insert": "CANVAS_STYLE_CONTROLS",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". It shows one preview card per theme, then every token of the active theme in collapsible groups: numbers as a slider with an exact input, colors as a swatch with a text field that keeps alpha, selects as segmented controls, booleans as switches, and one ink row per palette color. Rows honor "
        },
        {
          "insert": "visibleWhen",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", and an overridden row that "
        },
        {
          "insert": "visibleWhen",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " hides stays listed, dimmed, so it can still be reset. An override dot resets one token, and Reset theme clears the active theme's overrides."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-studio-style-why-20": {
      "id": "b-studio-style-why-20",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": a rail generated from the controls table exposes every token with no per-token UI code, so a token added to the style model appears in Studio by itself. The rejected alternative was a hand-built control per token, which lags the model it edits."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-studio-style-applies-21": {
      "id": "b-studio-style-applies-21",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "src/style/",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/studio/src/style",
              "label": "src/style/"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", including every future token or theme, which needs no change here."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-studio-settings-decision-25": {
      "id": "b-studio-settings-decision-25",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "use-canvas-style-settings.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/studio/src/style/use-canvas-style-settings.ts",
              "label": "use-canvas-style-settings.ts"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " owns the settings state: optimistic edits, a debounced PUT of the whole settings document, a localStorage copy for the first frame, and external changes pushed over the dev server. It also tracks the style the server last confirmed, and board-list thumbnails key their preview URLs on that style rather than on the local one."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-studio-settings-why-26": {
      "id": "b-studio-settings-why-26",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": a thumbnail keyed on an edit the server has not saved yet would fetch the old render and cache it under the new key, so it would never refresh. The rejected alternative was keying thumbnails on the local style."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-studio-settings-applies-27": {
      "id": "b-studio-settings-applies-27",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "use-canvas-style-settings.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/studio/src/style/use-canvas-style-settings.ts",
              "label": "use-canvas-style-settings.ts"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "App.tsx",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", including every future surface that caches a server render of a board."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-studio-panels-decision-28": {
      "id": "b-studio-panels-decision-28",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": the editor route opens one right-hand panel at a time: the Style rail, the editor's Inspector, or the agent sidebar. The editor mounts the rail in its "
        },
        {
          "insert": "sidePanel",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " slot, outside the stage, and shows its own Inspector when "
        },
        {
          "insert": "showInspector",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is set, which Studio's Inspect toggle drives. The Inspector edits a selection's detail line and its glyph: an icon's Glyph field, and a section's Icon field with a None choice."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-studio-panels-why-29": {
      "id": "b-studio-panels-why-29",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": a panel inside the stage, as a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "screenOverlay",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is, hit-tests clicks against the board under it and pans the board on a wheel scroll. A side panel in the editor's chrome keeps those events off the board, and editor popups stack above it. The rejected alternative was mounting the rail as a stage overlay."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-studio-panels-applies-30": {
      "id": "b-studio-panels-applies-30",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "App.tsx",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "'s editor route and the editor's "
        },
        {
          "insert": "sidePanel",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " slot, including every future settings panel, which mounts there and joins the one-open-at-a-time rule."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-studio-boards-heading": {
      "id": "b-studio-boards-heading",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Every Board Surface Receives the Resolved Style"
